--   An operator on a subfamily of the selected bits is the operator with the restricted strides
-- statement:
--   **An operator on a subfamily of the selected bits is the operator with the restricted strides.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFNSel`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFN.selOpF_subOp {g : κ → ι} (hg : Function.Injective g) (st : ι → ℕ) (n : ℕ)
--       (T : Matrix (κ → Fin 2) (κ → Fin 2) ℂ) (xs : List M) :
--       selOpF st n (subOp g T) xs = selOpF (st ∘ g) n T xs
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFN: selected-bit operators by record strides*: A selected-bit operator on a record array only needs, for every selected bit `i`, its record
--   stride `st i`: bit `i` of record `j` is `j / st i % 2` (`fbit`), and setting the selected bits to
--   `y` moves to record `fset st j y = j + Σ_i (y_i - bit_i) st_i`.  `selOpF st n T xs` is the
--   selected-bit operator in these terms.
--
